course: dictionary
lesson: 5032
title: Inheritance: money, genes and the past
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: «Inheritance» is a noun, and one word can have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning to use. «An inheritance is money or belongings left by someone who has died, as written in their will.» The clues are died and will, so here inheritance means money or things left behind after a death.
explain: In science, inheritance means the passing of features from parents to children through genes. Eye colour is an example. The clue here is that genes belong to biology, not to a will. Ask yourself: is this sentence about money, about biology, or about the past?
explain: Stories and history use inheritance in a wider way. «They grew like a snowball rolling downhill, picking up land by war, by marriage, by inheritance and by deals.» The land was passed down through families, so inheritance here means getting something from earlier generations. Use the swap check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Inheritance is a noun, and it is usually uncountable: you say some inheritance, not an inheritance, unless you mean a single gift or amount.
fact: «Inheritance» can mean money, property or things left by someone who has died.
fact: In science, inheritance means the passing of features from parents to children through genes.
fact: Something passed down from the past, such as customs, ideas or traditions, is called a cultural inheritance.
fact: Clue words such as will, died, genes and passed down show you which meaning of inheritance is being used.
exercise: «An inheritance is money or belongings left by someone who has died, as written in their will.» What does inheritance mean in this sentence? | A loan from the bank | A prize won in a race | A trip to a new country | *Money or belongings left by someone who has died
exercise: In science class, Ravi learns that eye colour is passed from parents to children through genes. What does inheritance mean in this science sense? | *The passing of features from parents to children through genes | Something you lose | Money left in a will | A school book
exercise: «They grew like a snowball rolling downhill, picking up land by war, by marriage, by inheritance and by deals.» Which way of getting land is named in the sentence? | by counting | by painting | *by inheritance | by swimming
test: «The prodigal son asked for his inheritance.» What did he ask for? | A school trip | A new coat | *His share of his father's money and property | A promise to be quiet
test: In «our cultural inheritance», what does inheritance mean? | A long walk | Money in the bank | *Something passed down from the past | Eye colour
exam: In «An inheritance is money or belongings left by someone who has died, as written in their will», which clue word shows that the meaning is about law and money? | belongings | *will | money | died
